&lt;ol style=&quot;margin-top:0cm&quot; start=&quot;2&quot; type=&quot;1&quot;&gt;
 &lt;/ol&gt;&lt;p&gt;The proposal is out of character with the existing, surrounding family homes within the immediate vicinity of the application site. The proposal therefore results in a detrimental impact to the character of the area. The proposal is therefore contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2026), policies D3.D(7), D3.D(9), and D3.D(10) and D14 of The London Plan (2021), policies GR1, HO10 of the Harrow local Plan 2021-2041&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ol style=&quot;margin-top:0cm&quot; start=&quot;2&quot; type=&quot;1&quot;&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;ol style=&quot;margin-top:0cm&quot; start=&quot;1&quot; type=&quot;1&quot;&gt;
 &lt;/ol&gt;&lt;p&gt;The use of the property as a 6-person HMO, by reason of the excessive number of occupiers that it accommodates, together with the failure to meet the minimum floorspace requirement (as originally built) set out in Harrow’s Local Plan Policy HO10, represents an overly intensive use of the site which results in substandard living accommodation for existing and future occupiers, and gives rise to undue levels of disturbance and noise resulting in a detrimental impact on the amenities of current, future occupiers and adjoining properties. &amp;nbsp;The proposal is therefore contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2026), policies D3.D(9), and D3.D(10) and D14 of The London Plan (2021), policies GR1 and HO10 of the Harrow local Plan 2021-2041&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ol style=&quot;margin-top:0cm&quot; start=&quot;1&quot; type=&quot;1&quot;&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
